WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.830
Though Rick Riordan's Percy Jackson series
is intended for younger audiences, there's

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:07.960
quite a bit for more seasoned viewers to pick
up on.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:12.331
From mythological mistakes to surprising musical
references, here are the things in the Percy

00:00:12.331 --> 00:00:16.230
Jackson movies that only adults would find
unobscured by the Mist.

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:21.490
For a movie based entirely around Greek mythology,
The Lightning Thief doesn't always pay as

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:24.099
much attention to its source material as it
should.

00:00:24.099 --> 00:00:27.989
We could forgive a few approximations and
omissions here and there, but there's one

00:00:27.989 --> 00:00:32.140
glaring inconsistency that undermines the
entire plot of the film.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.620
Persephone shouldn't have even been in the
Underworld when Percy and his friends arrived

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:37.320
there around the summer solstice.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:41.410
According to her own mythology, she's forced
to remain in her husband's domain during the

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:42.410
winter months.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:46.010
In the spring and summer months, she brings
mild weather to the Earth above.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:50.530
In fact, the entire quest for the pearls,
which takes up the bulk of the film, is inspired

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:54.600
by Persephone's captivity in the Underworld,
as the pearls belong to her and allow the

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.650
user to travel to and from Hell.

00:00:56.650 --> 00:01:00.960
The movie references her imprisonment frequently
but neglects to portray it accurately.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.280
It might not have been so big of an issue
if it wasn't Persephone who ended up securing

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.930
the gang's escape from the Underworld by knocking
out her own husband.

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:13.580
In reality, she wouldn't have even been there,
and they would've had a much harder time getting

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:14.580
out.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:18.450
While the movies are controversial among fans
of the books, we've got to give the Percy

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:22.760
Jackson films props for showcasing quite a
bit of disability representation.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:27.200
In fact, characteristics we'd associate with
disabilities are some of the primary identifiers

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.720
that mark a demigod.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:33.060
Percy has been told that he suffers from ADHD
and dyslexia because his brain is hardwired

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:36.950
for a drastically different world than the
high school landscape of required reading

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:41.490
and standardized tests, making it seem like
he has dysfunctions in a place he wasn't made

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:42.490
for.

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:46.790
The "impulsivity" attributed to ADHD is actually
a manifestation of his combat reflexes, and

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:51.060
the confusion that arises when he tries to
read English results from his natural predisposition

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:53.939
toward reading a notoriously difficult language.

00:01:53.939 --> 00:01:58.700
Grover and Chiron both have physical disabilities
in their disguised human forms, as well, and

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:02.180
these two mask underlying strengths and unique
abilities.

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:06.350
Chiron's wheelchair is a camouflaging vessel
for the magnificent horse portion of his centaur

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:11.389
body, and Grover's crutches allow him to mask
the fact that he, as a satyr, has goat legs

00:02:11.389 --> 00:02:13.930
that serve him well as Percy's protector.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:17.590
Percy's entire introduction to the demigod
world is based around the ideas that there's

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:22.170
more to life than meets the eye and that there's
a profound strength of character hiding in

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:23.170
anyone.

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:27.359
When it comes to being sensitive to individuals
of diverse backgrounds, the terminology that

00:02:27.359 --> 00:02:31.939
Percy learns to apply to the demigod world
deals with similar issues to that of human

00:02:31.939 --> 00:02:32.939
discourse.

00:02:32.939 --> 00:02:36.329
He learns the proper way of addressing and
referring to certain "demi-graphics," so to

00:02:36.329 --> 00:02:40.230
speak, with the help of his best friend and
guide, Grover, a satyr.

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:43.529
Apparently, "protector" duties include making
sure your charge doesn't say anything that

00:02:43.529 --> 00:02:47.919
will get him into trouble, which makes sense
when the wrath of mythical creatures is involved.

00:02:47.919 --> 00:02:51.599
It's also just something that good friends
do for each other — hold each other accountable

00:02:51.599 --> 00:02:54.099
for using oppressive or offensive language.

00:02:54.099 --> 00:02:58.129
One of the first suggestions that Grover offers
relates to his own identity, when he informs

00:02:58.129 --> 00:03:02.709
Percy that the "politically correct" term
for a half-man, half-goat is a satyr.

00:03:02.709 --> 00:03:06.470
Grover apprises his friend of the proper language
in other scenarios as well.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:11.499
For example, the preferred way to refer to
a cyclops, we learn, is "ocularly challenged."

00:03:12.499 --> 00:03:16.599
In the series, we meet the children of various
gods, and these immortal progeny share similar

00:03:16.599 --> 00:03:20.489
characteristics with their classical parents
— traits that younger audiences might not

00:03:20.489 --> 00:03:21.739
be familiar with.

00:03:21.739 --> 00:03:25.859
For example, Clarisse — an antagonist turned
ally of Percy's in Sea of Monsters – is

00:03:25.859 --> 00:03:30.339
a daughter of Ares, which is part of where
she gets the aggression and competitive spirit

00:03:30.339 --> 00:03:32.420
that initially makes her such a bitter rival.

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:35.140
Ares' children are pretty formidable in general.

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:38.879
In The Lightning Thief, during the infamous
game of "capture the flag" where the son of

00:03:38.879 --> 00:03:42.469
Poseidon first proves his mettle, Luke Castellan
warns Percy:

00:03:42.469 --> 00:03:44.469
"Sons of Ares, watch out."

00:03:44.469 --> 00:03:48.590
This alludes to the offspring of the god of
war and their inherently violent nature.

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:53.120
The daughters of Aphrodite, the goddess of
love, have also clearly inherited some personality

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:54.309
traits from their mother.

00:03:54.309 --> 00:03:57.979
Living together in the house under her name,
they behave like a sorority, spending their

00:03:57.979 --> 00:04:00.389
time tanning, flirting, and throwing parties.

00:04:00.389 --> 00:04:04.049
Allusions like this to the personality traits
of the gods are a little more subtle than,

00:04:04.049 --> 00:04:06.750
say, the son of Poseidon being able to heal
himself with water.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:12.319
Something odd is going on at the Lotus Casino
in Las Vegas, but only older viewers would

00:04:12.319 --> 00:04:16.690
understand the true nature of the lotus flower
cookies that Percy and his friends can't seem

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:17.690
to get enough of.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:21.470
These addictive, brightly colored sweets represent
something much darker.

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:25.290
The way the teenagers behave after consuming
them and the effects they have on the user's

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:29.820
mood, intellect, and the passage of time render
them a clear reference to party drugs and

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:30.820
narcotics.

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:34.650
The delicacies take their inspiration from
the myth of the Lotus-Eaters, which describes

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:38.720
a tribe of people encountered by Odysseus
on his famous quest, people who offered the

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:43.320
hero and his crew a mysterious plant that
caused them to drift into a state of mindless

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:44.910
bliss outside of time.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:50.290
This is certainly what happens to Percy, Annabeth,
and Grover in Las Vegas, a city synonymous

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:51.940
with indulgence and excess.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:58.340
Mr. D — as the attendees at Camp Half-Blood
call Dionysus, the god of wine, madness, and

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:01.900
parties — is the newly appointed camp director
in Sea of Monsters.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:06.060
This position comes as part of a punishment
Zeus whipped up to get back at his son for

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:10.590
going against the bro code and pursuing a
dryad Zeus had a fancy for.

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:14.590
But the worst of Dionysus' punishment was
the fact that every time he attempted to pour

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:17.660
himself a glass of wine, it turned into water
in his cup.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:21.380
In response to his curse, he comments that
Christians have a guy who can do that trick

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:25.220
in reverse, a reference to Jesus turning water
into wine in the Bible.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:30.270
Not only can he not drink any wine, he can't
use his powers to grow grapes for wine, either.

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:34.780
In the books, it's hinted that a prior period
of punishment caused the Prohibition era,

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:36.970
which is also a decidedly adult allusion.

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:42.560
Numerous nods to the real world exist in this
series in addition to Biblical and mythological

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:45.860
references, and it's likely that they pass
right over children.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:50.110
For instance, kids probably don't notice the
Maserati in which Percy and his friends escape

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:51.420
from the Lotus Casino.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:55.640
And they probably won't know that the trident
logo for the luxury car brand was, in fact,

00:05:55.640 --> 00:06:00.130
based on Percy's father — or at least his
Roman counterpart, Neptune, and the fountain

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:04.490
dedicated to his likeness in the company's
home city of Bologna, Italy.

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:08.470
Another motor vehicle from The Lightning Thief
carries its own special significance.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:12.990
When the heroes get off their bus amidst the
sounds of AC/DC's "Highway to Hell," the front

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:15.810
of the bus indicates that it's bound for Atlantic
City.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:20.720
As you may know, Atlantic City has a hellish
reputation among many adults, and is negatively

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:22.810
portrayed in numerous films and shows.

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:28.240
The camera tracks quickly to close in on the
suave ruler of the Underworld, so quickly

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:32.980
that we almost miss it, but eagle-eyed fans
have pointed out that Hades can be seen in

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:37.000
possession of a Gibson SG guitar when we first
meet him in his palace.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:41.750
This bright red axe is the same type of guitar
as Angus Young's, the lead guitarist of AC/DC.

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:46.030
One of the band's most famous songs is "Highway
to Hell," which for Hades would simply be

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:47.480
the highway home.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:52.150
The god's persona in the film rocks pretty
hard, as well, from the unruly curls and goatee

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:55.710
to the leather bracelet and aesthetically
ripped black sleeves.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:59.610
Even more fittingly, the logo of the iconic
rock band features a lightning bolt where

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:03.480
the forward slash would be -- a nod to Zeus'
lightning bolt, which Percy is accused of

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:04.920
stealing in The Lightning Thief.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:10.190
If The Lightning Thief did a good job with
disability representation, Sea of Monsters

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:15.470
built on that legacy by showcasing the difficulty
of growing up and the insidious nature of

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:16.470
impostor syndrome.

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:20.620
That's when the sufferer believes that they're
inadequate and experiences exaggerated doubt

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:23.420
about their achievements despite evidence
of success.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:27.200
Percy actually says out loud that he sometimes
doesn't believe he actually did the things

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:28.240
he was praised for.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:31.800
This lack of belief is actually a symptom
of severe imposter syndrome.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:36.270
For Percy to say it in such clear terms is
surely comforting to high achievers who suffer

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:38.180
from this illusive mental ailment.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:43.290
The Mist is a magical force that prevents
mortals -- and sometimes demigods, if it's

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:47.500
strong enough -- from seeing gods, monsters,
and other supernatural entities by disguising

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.510
them as something from the mortal world.

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:54.389
For example, such magic is at work disguising
Chiron's centaur body as a wheelchair.

00:07:54.389 --> 00:07:58.760
In order to allow him to travel seamlessly
with the group of demigods in Sea of Monsters,

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:03.360
Annabeth procures a spray bottle of Mist that
artificially disguises Tyson, making him look

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:06.260
like a human with two eyes rather than a cyclops.

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:10.930
Hilariously, the side effects listed on the
bottle are a joke at the expense of medication

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:15.030
commercials that spout off a slew of side
effects that are sometimes so contradictory

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:18.560
that they do the opposite of what the medicine
itself is supposed to do.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:22.480
"Side effects may include handsomeness, headache,
self esteem, and low self-esteem"

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:27.100
Sea of Monsters builds upon the deep discussion
of its predecessor by exploring Annabeth's

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:29.100
prejudice against cyclopes.

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:32.919
Over the course of the film, Annabeth makes
her animosity toward Percy's half-brother,

00:08:32.919 --> 00:08:36.159
Tyson — as well as cyclopes in general — very
apparent.

00:08:36.159 --> 00:08:40.469
However, we don't really learn why until later
in the story when she opens up about how it

00:08:40.469 --> 00:08:44.139
was a cyclops who took the life of her friend,
Thalia, years ago.

00:08:44.139 --> 00:08:47.939
To complicate matters further, one of the
biggest obstacles in the film's storyline

00:08:47.939 --> 00:08:53.279
is yet another cyclops, from whom they must
rescue Grover, as well as the magical Golden

00:08:53.279 --> 00:08:54.279
Fleece.

00:08:54.279 --> 00:08:57.610
The circumstances make it very easy for Annabeth
to cling to her personal prejudice, given

00:08:57.610 --> 00:09:01.550
that the cyclopean threat to their mission
only serves to reinforce it.

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:05.370
Despite this, however, Annabeth undergoes
a personal journey in tandem with the physical

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:08.940
one, a transformation that holds a lesson
for viewers of all ages.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:14.370
She gradually learns to dismantle her discriminatory
paradigms and behaviors against cyclopes,

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:18.610
finally acknowledging that it's destructive
to make assumptions about and harbor aggression

00:09:18.610 --> 00:09:21.160
toward an entire group of people.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:25.350
The Gray Sisters — Anger, Wasp, and Tempest
— make their first appearance in Sea of

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:27.999
Monsters, sharing only one eye between them.

00:09:27.999 --> 00:09:32.980
This deficiency automatically makes the trio
an ideal slapstick choice to drive a supernatural

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:33.980
taxicab.

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:37.480
As a result, we got a lot of inside jokes
and references thanks to these siblings.

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:41.720
For example, Annabeth announces their vessel
as a Chariot of Damnation, prompting Grover

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:44.420
to reply that it looks like a New York City
cab.

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:47.839
Annabeth retorts, "Same difference," which
is sure to get a chuckle out of any adult

00:09:47.839 --> 00:09:49.430
who's taken a bad cab ride.

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:53.759
The sisters also bemoan a familiar mortal
woe — that of a terrible driver's license

00:09:53.759 --> 00:09:54.759
picture.

00:09:54.759 --> 00:09:58.430
But while our unflattering photos typically
amount to a washed-out face or an awkward

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:02.589
blink, the crime committed by the Graeae's
portrait is much more offensive.

00:10:02.589 --> 00:10:06.889
And if you look closely with your own eyes,
however many you have, it also looks like,

00:10:06.889 --> 00:10:11.470
from the suspiciously serpentine hair, the
bobblehead on the dashboard is a likeness

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:12.470
of Medusa.

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:16.569
In mythology, the Graeae are the ones who
give the hero Perseus the information he needs

00:10:16.569 --> 00:10:18.430
to kill Medusa, by beheading her.

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:20.899
Hermes works for the UPS Store.

00:10:20.899 --> 00:10:24.480
That's pretty fitting for the "herald of the
gods," who worked as a messenger and courier

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:29.240
for Mount Olympus and was also the bringer
of good luck and god of wealth, trade, travel,

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:30.240
and language.

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:34.860
The portrayal by Nathan Fillion in Sea of
Monsters captures a subtle blend of matter-of-factness

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:38.339
and mischief that only the deftest of gods
could pull off.

00:10:38.339 --> 00:10:42.279
As the god of numerous ubiquitous things,
it's fitting that many of Hermes' artifacts

00:10:42.279 --> 00:10:45.029
show up as widely used symbols even today.

00:10:45.029 --> 00:10:49.190
We can recognize his winged feet in the Goodyear
logo, as the company thought that the god

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:53.020
Mercury -- who is the Roman version of Hermes
-- held many of the qualities they wanted

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:54.660
their company to be known for.

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:59.500
And honestly, the god of trade and commerce
was a great choice to represent the tire company.

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:03.800
Hermes' staff is also widely used as a symbol
in the United States, representing medicine,

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:08.220
which is definitely a field in which we want
the bringer of good luck on our side.

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:10.339
